    "ssky_faqs_HdbVR3": {
      "type": "ssky-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_eEyWqT": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>Frequently Asked Questions about Economics for Kids</p>",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold"
          }
        },
        "faq_6FJEmp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Long Does It Usually Take for a Child to Understand Economics?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>This depends on the child’s age and reading level, but most begin to grasp key ideas within a few weeks of regular reading and discussion. Our books and resources have fun storytelling that helps concepts click faster with your kids than traditional textbooks.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_V9rrQp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>What Is the Best Age to Start Teaching Children Basic Economics Concepts Like Saving and Budgeting?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>A good starting point is ages 5 to 7. At this stage, kids are ready to understand simple ideas like saving for a toy or choosing between two treats. The earlier they start, the stronger their financial habits will be.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_mzaVfE": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Can I Introduce Topics Such as Supply and Demand or Trade In a Fun, Kid-Friendly Way?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Stories and hands-on activities work best. For example, our books explain these ideas through exciting adventures and relatable scenarios like lemonade stands or community markets.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_j84J3D": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Are There Simple Activities or Games That Help Children Understand Money Management and Decision-Making?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! Set up a pretend store, encourage a mini business like selling crafts, or play board games involving buying and selling. These interactive experiences make lessons stick.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_FcWqtm": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Can I Explain the Value of Money and the Difference Between Needs and Wants to Young Children?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Use real-life examples. Show how groceries are needs while toys are wants. Our books reinforce these ideas through memorable characters and fun, everyday situations.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_WX3UqE": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Looking for Something Else?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>We also have a wide range of resources and books for children, no matter what stage or age they’re at. You can explore our colorful <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/toddler-books\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">toddler books</span></a>, engaging <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/books-for-teens\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">books for teens</span></a>, or our exciting <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/bundles\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">book bundles</span></a> to keep your kids entertained for hours.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
